From 8eb10742be1b8381d39f94363f3662d19b8a3bef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zortos <zortosdev@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:58:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] frame gen: coarse-to-fine block matching for Lichii
 Optical Flow (#2386)

* frame gen: coarse-to-fine block matching for Lichii Optical Flow

Port sheepbun/lichii-bunx2 0125458acc (luma pyramid, coarse full search,
refinement around coarser motion, sub-pixel fit, static-pixel and sample
validity checks) with 5x5 blocks. Where the warped samples disagree, show
the nearer real frame instead of blending them, and drop the unwarped
blend that drew both positions of moving outlines.

* frame gen: warp static-looking pixels an object crossed, keep the real frame where both warps are rejected

* frame gen: drop the crossing and both-rejected changes to the interpolation

The crossing branch replaced a thin static overlay with warped background
during a pan, and with the check that prevents that it no longer paid off.
Showing the nearer real frame where both warps are rejected measured worse
on sprite walks than blending them.

* frame gen: compare flow blocks without their mean

Fades and menu transitions change the brightness of the whole scene, and
the absolute block cost then picked arbitrary offsets up to the pyramid's
192 px range, which warped the generated frames. Zero-mean blocks match
through the brightness change.
